# 000300-000399/20070327T041845Z_118185041.wiki
zΔ⚡b|=2f3|-1|+The d|=4|+ut|=1|+lity wa|=2|+developed in the e|=1|+rly 1970s on|=2|+he [[Unix]] op|=2|+ating syste|=2|+which was emerging from [[AT&T]] [[Bell Labs]] in M|=1|+rray Hill, New Jer|=2|+y.  The final version, first shippe|=2|+w|=1|+th the 5th Editio|=2|-1|+of Unix in 1974, was |=3|+irely written by [[D|=1|+uglas McIlroy]].  This research was published i|=2|+a 1976 paper co%2Dwritten with [[James |=1|+. Hunt]] who developed |=1|+n initial prototype of diff.%0A%0AMcIlroy'|=1|+ work was preceded and influenced by [[Step|=1|+en C. Johnson%7CSteve Johnson]]'s compar|=1|+so|=1|+ pro|=1|+ram on [[GECOS]] and [[Mike Lesk]]'s <|=1|+t>proof</tt> program.  <tt>proof</tt> also originated |=3|+Unix and, like diff, produced line%2Dby%2Dline changes and even used angle%2Dbrackets (">" and "<") for presenting line insertions and deletions in |=2|+e progr|=1|+m's ou|=1|+put.|=1|+ The [[heur|=2|+tic]]s|=1|+used in t|=1|+ese early appl|=1|+cations were, however, deemed unreliable.  The potential usefulness of a diff tool provoked McIlroy into researchin|=1|+ and designing a more robust tool t|=1|+at cou|=1|+d be used in a variet|=4|+ tasks but per|=1|+orm w|=1|+ll i|=1|+ the pro|=1|+essing and size limitations of the [[PDP%2D11]]'s hardware.  His approach to the problem resulted from collaboration also with ind|=2|+iduals at B|=1|+ll Labs including [[Alfred Aho]], [[Elliot Pinson]], [[Jeffrey Ullman]], and [[Harold S. Stone]].%0A%0AIn the context of Unix, the use of the <tt>[[ed (Unix)%7Ced]]</tt> line editor provided diff with the natural ability to create machine%2Dusable "edit scripts"|=6|+se edit scripts, when saved to a file, can, along with the|=8|+l file, be reconstituted by <tt>ed</tt> in|=2|+ the modified file in its enti|=1|+ety.|=1|+ Th|=3|-1|+great|=1|+y r|=1|-1|+duced the [[secondary storage]] necessary to maintain multiple versions of a file. |=2|+cIlroy considered writing |=1|+ post%2Dpro|=1|-1|+essor for diff where |=1|+ vari|=1|+ty of output formats could be designed|=5|+implemented, but |=3|+found i|=1|+ more frugal and simpler to |=1|+ave diff be resp|=1|+nsible for generating the syntax and reverse%2Dorder inp|=1|+t accepted by the <tt>ed</tt> command.%0AIn 1985, [[Larry Wall]] composed a separate utility, [[patch (Unix)%7Cpatch]], that |=1|+eneralized and extended t|=1|+e abili|=1|+y|=1|+t|=1|+ modi|=1|+y|=1|+files wi|=2|+ d|=1|+ff output.  Mode|=2|+in [[Emacs]] also allow for converting the format of patches an|=1|+ even editing patches interactively.%0A%0AIn diff's early years, common |=1|+ses included compa|=5|+ch|=1|+nges in the|=2|+ource of software code and markup for technica|=1|+ docum|=1|+nts, v|=1|+rifying |=1|+rogram debugging|=2|-1|+utput, comparing filesystem listings and analyzing comput|=4|+ssembly code.  The outpu|=2|+t|=1|+rgeted|=2|+o|=1|+ <tt>ed</tt> was mot|=1|+vat|=1|+d to provide compressio|=1|+ for a sequence of mo|=1|+ification|=2|+made to a file.  T|=1|+e [[SCCS%7CS|=2|+rce Code Control Sy|=1|+t|=1|+m]] (SCCS) emerged|=4|+the late 1970s as a |=1|+ir|=2|+t cons|=1|+quence of this develop|=1|-1|+ent.%0A%0AA conceptual predec|=1|+sso|=5|-1|+diff includes [[Project Xanadu]], a hypertext project established in 196|=1|-3|+ that had envisioned a version tracking system necessary for|=1|+its|=1|+"transp|=1|+in|=1|+ing windows" feature.  T|=2|+ featu|=1|+e|=1|+subsumed file differences in the expansi|=1|+e term "[[tr|=1|+nsclusion]]", whe|=1|+e a document has |=1|+ncluded in it p|=1|+rts of o|=1|+her documents or revis|=4|+.%0A%0AIn|=1|+the digit|=1|+l |=2|+alm|=1|+of the humanities, com|=1|+uter c|=1|+mpa|=1|+ison sys|=1|+ems were understood to have been created for working on |=1|+iterar|=2|+works publishe|=1|+ as large volumes.{{huh}}{{Fact%7Cdate%3DMarch 2007}}%0A%0A%3D%3D Usage %3D%3D%0A%0AIt |=1|+s invoked |=1|+rom the command line with the names o|=1|-1|+ two|=2|+iles: <tt>diff ''original''  ''new''</tt>.  The o|=1|+tput of the |=1|+ommand represents the changes required to ma|=1|+e the ''orig|=2|+al'' file become the ''new'' file.%0A%0AIf ''ori|=1|+inal'' and ''new'' are directories, then|=5|+ will be run on each file that exists in both directories.  An option|=2|+<tt>%2Dr</tt>, will d|=1|+scend any ma|=2|-2|+hing|=1|+subdirectories to compare files|=2|+etween directories.%0A%0AAn|=1|+ of|=5|+examples in the article use the follo|=1|+ing two files,  ''origin|=1|+l'' and ''new'':%0A%0A{%7C class%3D"prett|=1|+table"%0A%7C%2D|=1|+v|=2|+ign%3D"top"%0A%7C%0A''original'':%0A%0A  This part of th|=1|-1|+%0A |=1|+docu|=1|+ent h|=1|+s stayed the%0A  same from version to%0A  version.  It shouldn't%0A  be shown if it doesn't%0A  |=1|+hange.  Othe|=1|+wise, th|=1|+t%0A  would not b|=2|+helping to%0A  comp|=1|+ess the size of the%0A  changes.%0A  %0A  This paragraph contains%0A  text that is o|=1|+tdated.%0A  It will be de|=2|+ted in the%0A  near future.%0A  %0A  It i|=2|+important to spell%0A  check this dokument. On%0A  the other hand, a%0A  misspelled word isn't%0A  the end of |=b|-2|+  Nothing in the|=1|-1|+re|=1|+t of%0A  this par|=2|+raph needs to%0A  be changed. Things can%0A  b|=2|-2|+added after it.|=1|+%7C |=1|+''new'':%0A%0A  |=8|+an important%0A  notice! It sho|=1|+ld%0A  therefore be located at%0A  the beginning of thi|=1|+%0A  docum|=1|+nt!%0A  %0A  This part of the%0A  |=1|+ocument|=1|+has stayed the%0A  same from version to%0A  version.  It shouldn't%0A  be sho|=1|+n if it doesn't%0A  c|=1|-1|+a|=1|+ge. |=1|+O|=4|+wis|=1|+,|=1|+that%0A  would not be help|=1|+ng to%0A  compres|=2|+anything.%0A  %0A  It i|=1|+ imp|=1|+rtant to spell%0A  check this docu|=2|+nt. On%0A  the |=1|+ther ha|=1|+d, a%0A  misspell|=1|+d word isn't%0A|=1|-1|+ the end |=1|+f the world.%0A  Nothing in the rest of%0A  this paragraph needs to%0A  be changed. Things can%0A  be added after it.%0A  %0A  This paragraph contains%0A  important new additions%0A  to this doc|=1|+ment.%0A%7C}%0A%0AThe|=1|+command <tt>diff o|=1|+iginal n|=1|+w</tt> produces the following ''norm|=2|+ diff output'':%0A%0A  0a1,6%0A  > This is an important%0A  > notice! It shou|=1|-1|+d%0A  >|=1|+t|=1|+erefore be loc|=3|+d|=2|+t%0A  > the begi|=1|+ning of this%0A  > |=1|+ocument!%0A|=1|+ >%0A  8,14c14%0A  < compress the size o|=1|+ th|=1|+%0A  < chang|=1|+s.%0A  <%0A  < This paragraph contains%0A  < text that is outdated.%0A  < It wi|=1|+l be|=1|+de|=1|+eted |=1|+n the%0A  < near future.%0A  %2D%2D%2D%0A  > compress anything.%0A  17c17%0A  < chec|=1|+ this dokum|=1|+nt. On%0A  %2D%2D%2D%0A  > check|=1|+th|=1|+s docume|=1|+t. On%0A  24a25,28%0A  >%0A  > Thi|=1|+ paragraph contains%0A  > important new additions%0A  > to this doc|=1|+ment.%0A%0AIn this traditiona|=1|+ ou|=1|+put format, '''a''' stands for ''added'', '''d''' for ''deleted'' and '''c''' for ''changed''.  L|=2|+e numbers of the ori|=1|+inal file appear before a/d/c and|=3|+os|=1|+ of the |=1|+odified file appear after|=3|+[[Angle bracket]]s appear at |=2|+e beg|=1|+nning of line|=3|+hat ar|=1|+ added, deleted o|=1|-1|+ changed.  Addition|=1|+l|=1|+ne|=3|+re|=1|+added to the o|=1|+iginal fil|=1|+ to a|=1|+pear in the new fi|=1|+e. Deletion lines |=1|-1|+re delet|=1|+d fro|=1|+ th|=1|+ origi|=1|+al file |=1|+o be missing in the new|=2|+ile.%0A%0ABy default, lines c|=1|+mmon to both files a|=1|+e|=1|-1|+not shown.  Lines that have moved will show |=1|+p as added on their new lo|=1|-1|+ation and as deleted on their old location.%0A%0A%3D%3D Variations %3D%3D%0A%0AMost diff|=1|+implementations remain outwardl|=1|+ unchanged since 1975.  The m|=1|+difications incl|=1|+de|=1|+improvements to the c|=2|+e|=1|-1|+alg|=1|+rithm, the addition of useful feat|=2|+es|=1|+to the comm|=1|+nd, and|=1|+t|=1|+e design |=1|+f n|=1|+w output formats|=2|+The|=1|-1|+basic alg|=1|-1|+rithm|=1|-1|+i|=1|+ d|=1|+scribed|=2|+n |=1|+he papers|=1|+''An O(ND) Difference A|=1|+gor|=1|-1|+thm and its Variations'' by Eugene W. My|=1|+rs and in ''A File Comparison Program'' by Webb Miller and Myers.  The algorithm|=2|+as independently discovered and described in ''Algorit|=1|+ms for Approximat|=1|+ Stri|=1|+g|=1|+Matching'', b|=1|+ [[E. Ukk|=1|-1|+nen]].  The first editions of the diff program were designed for line|=2|+omp|=1|+risons of text fi|=1|+es expecting the [[new|=1|+ine]]|=1|-1|+character t|=1|+ deli|=1|+it lines.  By th|=1|+ 1980s, supp|=1|+rt for bi|=1|+ary fil|=1|+s resulted in|=3|+shift i|=1|+ the |=1|+pplication's design and imple|=2|+ntation|=2d53|
